OL,3,GNEWSAThe making of Moby Dick - when
OL,4,AHollywood came to a tiny Welsh harbour
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt is the seaside town that was
OL,7,Ftransformed in to Dylan Thomas's
OL,8,FLlareggub in 1971, but Fishguard was
OL,9,Falso the backdrop for another iconic
OL,10,Ffilm.
OL,12,FDirector John Huston chose the
OL,13,FPembrokeshire town as one of Moby
OL,14,FDick's locations, where the
OL,15,F19th-Century Nantucket whaling ship
OL,16,FPequod can be seen sailing.
OL,18,FThe film, released 70 years ago in
OL,19,F1956, starred Gregory Peck as Captain
OL,20,FAhab and at the time was one of
OL,21,FHollywood's most expensive films,
OL,22,Fcosting about $4m (#3m).
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
